id: pm-rust-context-history-output
title: Native richer history and canonical orientation continuations
description: "Complete history provenance, summaries and filters, diffs and fields; canonical orientation output include, budgets, sessions and cursors; remaining context filters, aliases and runtime intent declarations."
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 3
tags[2]: follow-up,orientation
created_at: "2026-11-06T09:16:11.304Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-06T17:13:38.307Z"
author: codex-astra
acceptance_criteria: "Every projection and cursor matches a pinned oracle byte-exact in JSON and TOON; cover history integrity, missing streams, stale cursor replay, custom intent precedence and filters; preserve append-only history and work without git; retain typed refusals for unfinished contracts."
parent: pm-rust-s6j4
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T10:08:51.572Z",codex-astra,The November oracle changes default history to newest-first rows and adds total/order metadata. This slice keeps the independently pinned October history contract and does not claim current history parity; the follow-up must port default and richer projections together with exact current-oracle differentials.
  "2026-11-06T13:11:07.970Z",codex-astra,"Current-oracle review cases confirm three published recovery UX limitations retained for byte compatibility: receipt-only intent omission returns success status; its retry drops explicit sections and output controls; canonical context output cursors require the published CLI because native continuation remains unsupported. The generated reviewed-contract test executes the emitted intent retry and published output cursor, checks exact supported packets, and verifies the native typed refusal. Follow-up acceptance must preserve the requested projection while coordinating any changed receipt contract with the selected oracle version. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-11-06T17:13:38.304Z",codex-astra,"Additional acceptance criterion for settings-diagnostic parity: compare valid current settings, historical partial settings, and invalid context shapes against the pinned oracle in non-git trackers; preserve its settings_read_invalid_schema warning packets without writes. Until that warning contract is certified, native context must explicitly refuse invalid context-setting shapes while normal item reads and export remain available."
body: ""
